Queries and Sub Queries
=========================

Sub Queries
===========
what is sub query?
--------------------
-- A sub Query is query inside a another query
--It written inside parenthesis() and its result is used by the outer Query
--It is called as 
  -Inner Query
  -Nested Query
  -Inner Select

General Syntax
--------------
select column-list
from table
where column OPERATOR(Select column from table where condition)

Purpose of Sub Query
--------------------
--To break down complex problems into smaller queries
--To use the result of one query as input to another
--To avoid multiple steps(write in a single query instead of temp tables)

Types of Sub Query
--------------------
1.Single-row-subquery
2.multi-row-subquery
3.nested subquery
4.corelated subquery
5.exists/not exists subquery


Single-Row-Subquery
====================
-- Single row sub-queries returns exactly one row and one column.
They used comparision operators(<,>,<=,>=,==,1=)

**Characteristics
----------------
--returns only one value
--Can use single-value comparision operators
--If subquery returns no rows or multiple rows.it causes an error

Syntax:
-------
select column 
from table
where column opetator(select column from table where condition)


Multi-Row-Subquery
===================
(a).Multi-row subqueries with IN
-- A multi row subquery returns more than one row
the In operator is used when you want to compare a 
value with multiple values return by the subquery

**Characterstics
------------------
-- Returns Multi Rows
-- Use the In Operator
-- Checks if a value exists in the list returned by the subquery
-- Equivalent to multiple OR Conditions
-- Most Commonly used for matching values

Syntax
------
select column 
from table
where column IN(select column from table where condition)

(b).Multi-Row-Subquery(ANY/some)
-----------------------------------
-- Multi-row-subquery returns multiple rows when using ANY or SOME
The condition is true if it matches at least one value returned by the subquery

Chacterstics
-------------
-- Returns multiple rows
-- any and some are interchanged
-- condition is true if any of the values satisfy the condition
-- often used with IN,>ANY,<ANY,=ANY etc

Syntax:
-------
select column 
from table
where column ANY/SOME(select column from table where condition)


(c).Mutli-Row-Subquery(ALL)
--------------------------------
-- The All operator means the condition must be true for all values returned by the sub_query

Characterstics
---------------
--Condition Must be true for all values in the subquery result
--Often used with >all,<all,>=all,<=all
-- >all means greater than the maximum value
-- <all means less than the minimum value

Syntax:
--------
select column 
from table
where column ALL(select column from table where condition)


Nested Subquery
================
-- Nested Subqueries are the subqueries within subqueries
they can be  multiple levels deep and are executed from the innermost to the outermost

Characterstics
---------------
-- Multiple levels of nesting
-- inner queries execute first
-- can combine different types of subqueries
-- useful for complex conditions

Syntax:
--------
SELECT COLUMN-LIST FROM TABLE
WHERE COLUMN=(SELECT COLUMN
                 FROM TABLE
                   WHERE COLUMN=(SELECT
                                COLUMN FROM TABLE
                                         WHERE CONDITION));


Corelated Subquery
===================
-- Corelated SubQuries are Subqueries that references column from the outer query.
unlike regular subqueries that are execute once.corelated subqueries execute once
for each row proceed by the outer subquery

Characterstics
-----------------
-- reference column from the outer query
-- executes multiple times(once per outer row)
-- cannot be executed independently
-- often used with exists,not exists
-- generally slower than non_corelated subqueries

Syntax:
-------
select columns
from table1 outer_alias
where condition(select column
                  from table2 inner_alias
                          where inner_alias.column=outer_alias.column);


Exists/Not Exists Subquery
===========================
-- Exists is used to test whether a subqueries returns any rows
It returns true if the subquery returns at least one row,false otherwise
-- Not Existes return true if the subquery returns no rows

Characterstics
--------------
-- returns TRUE/FALSE (Boolean result)
-- More efficient than IN for large data sets
-- Often used with corelated subquries
-- stops execution as soon as first match is found
-- select clause is in exists doesn't matter

Syntax:
-------
SELECT COLUMNS
FROM TABLE
WHERE EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM TABLE2 WHERE  CONDITION);


Syntax:
-------
SELECT COLUMNS
FROM TABLE
WHERE NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM TABLE2 WHERE  CONDITION);





